1. **A computer-implemented method for grouping records distributed between a first database cluster and a second database cluster, the method comprising:**

   obtaining a plurality of distinct records associated with the first database cluster or the second database cluster;

   determining, for each distinct record, whether the distinct record has a first priority or a second priority;

   assigning each distinct record to one of a plurality of groups based at least in part on the determined priority, such that records having the first priority are associated with the first database cluster and records having the second priority are associated with the second database cluster; and

   storing or updating grouping information identifying the association of each distinct record with the corresponding group or database cluster.
